            <ArticleTitle>Predictors of recurrent abdominal pain among 9 to 15-year-old urban school-children in Malaysia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>353-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">A cross-sectional survey of school-children aged from 9 to 15 y was performed in the city of Petaling Jaya to look for predictors of recurrent abdominal pain. A sample of 1488 children was randomly chosen, of whom 143 (9.6%) had recurrent abdominal pain according to Apley's criteria.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The results of the study show that recurrent abdominal pain was associated with a number of demographic variables, a tendency to have other complaints and a family history of chronic abdominal complaints.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
